  "rules": {
    "summary": "Nine teams each play six series of two to five Tests, three at home and three away, from June 2025. A win is worth 12 points, a tie 6, a draw 4 and a loss 0. An abandoned Test is a draw, unless the pitch or outfield is rated unfit, when the visitors take the win's points. Each over short of the minimum rate costs a point. Teams are ranked by the percentage of available points they won (PCT), then series wins, away PCT and the ICC Test ranking at the end of the window. A Test not played for an accepted reason (a security or force-majeure ruling) is left out; one forfeited goes to the other side. The top two meet in the final at The Oval on 9-13 June 2027, with a reserve day; a drawn, tied or abandoned final makes them joint champions.",
